## Example Test Execution

```
TEST: 1.1 - Rename Method (Kotlin)

OPERATION:
- Tool: intellij_rename_symbol
- File: src/test/resources/testdata/kotlin/SampleClass.kt
- Line: 12
- Old Name: oldMethodName
- New Name: newMethodName

EXPECTED:
- Response: {"success": true, "filesChanged": [...], "changesCount": 1}
- Line 12 changes from "fun oldMethodName" to "fun newMethodName"

EXECUTE:
[Call MCP tool with parameters]

VERIFY:
- Response: ✅ success=true, changesCount=1
- Inline snippet: ✅ Line 12 shows "fun newMethodName"
- Full diff: ✅ Only line 12 changed

RESULT: ✅ PASS

Moving to Test 1.2...
```

## When to Ask User

Only interrupt the user if:
- Multiple tests fail with the same root cause and you're unsure of the fix
- A test failure suggests the test plan or expected files might be wrong
- The bug requires architectural changes
- You encounter an unexpected error you cannot resolve

Otherwise, continue iterating through fix → rebuild → deploy → test cycles until all tests pass.
